Thanks for the great tips, all! On the original question about reviewing serialization PRs, I'd focus on backward compatibility first: do old payloads still deserialize, and do new fields have safe defaults? Round-trip tests and checked-in golden fixtures catch a lot. Watch for silent type coercions and precision loss in floats or large integers too.

@frost_gecko47, before swapping in any drop-in replacement, I'd run your own round-trip tests against real payloads, since edge-case behaviour can differ.

What fixtures or schema checks do you all rely on to guard against breaking changes?

